{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files ComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552 && sed -n '1,100p' ComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/run-tests.py\"","aggregated_output":"ComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/rapier.module.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/retrofit.md\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/styles.css\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/hub-integration.md\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/session.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/three.tsl.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/bridge.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/hub-test.html\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/app.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/sim.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/test-audio.py\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/round.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/three.core.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/three.webgpu.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/harness.html\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/qa-plan.md\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/run-tests.py\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/view.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/index.html\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/audio.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/title.json\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/hub.js\nComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/README.md\n#!/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\n\"\"\"ComBop regression runner. Run this file directly from any directory.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport contextlib\nimport functools\nimport http.server\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport runpy\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport traceback\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Iterator\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import Browser, Page, sync_playwright\n\nPROJECT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nROOT = PROJECT.parent\nSLUG = PROJECT.name\nGAME = ROOT / f\"{SLUG}.html\"\nRESULT = PROJECT / \"test-results.json\"\nGPU_ARGS = [\n    \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n    \"--enable-features=Vulkan\",\n    \"--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\",\n    \"--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required\",\n]\n\n\nclass QuietHandler(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, format: str, *args: Any) -> None:\n        pass\n\n\n@contextlib.contextmanager\ndef local_server() -> Iterator[str]:\n    handler = functools.partial(QuietHandler, directory=str(ROOT))\n    server = http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", 0), handler)\n    thread = threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\n    thread.start()\n    try:\n        yield f\"http://127.0.0.1:{server.server_port}\"\n    finally:\n        server.shutdown()\n        server.server_close()\n        thread.join(timeout=5)\n\n\nclass Suite:\n    def __init__(\n        self, browser: Browser, origin: str, only: list[str] | None = None\n    ) -> None:\n        self.browser = browser\n        self.origin = origin\n        self.results: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n        self.started = time.monotonic()\n        self.only = only or []\n\n    def check(self, name: str, action: Callable[[], Any]) -> None:\n        if self.only and not any(\n            fragment.casefold() in name.casefold() for fragment in self.only\n        ):\n            return\n        start = time.monotonic()\n        try:\n            detail = action()\n            self.results.append(\n                {\n                    \"name\": name,\n                    \"pass\": True,\n                    \"seconds\": round(time.monotonic() - start, 2),\n                    \"detail\": detail,\n                }\n            )\n        except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - Keep running after an individual check fails.\n            message = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n            print(f\"FAIL {name}: {message}\", flush=True)\n            self.results.append(\n                {\n                    \"name\": name,\n                    \"pass\": False,\n                    \"seconds\": round(time.monotonic() - start, 2),\n                    \"error\": message,\n                    \"traceback\": traceback.format_exc(),\n                }\n            )\n\n    @contextlib.contextmanager\n    def page(\n        self, *, touch: bool = False, controller: bool = False, controllers: int = 1\n    ) -> Iterator[Page]:\n        context = self.browser.new_context(\n            viewport={\"width\": 844, \"height\": 390}\n            if touch\n            else {\"width\": 1600, \"height\": 900},\n            has_touch=touch,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The gameplay and menus are now implemented: ricochet previews, breakable crates, explosive fuel cans, automatic reloads, burst dodges, repairs, overdrive, and a closing hot zone. Standalone WebRTC has also passed a two-browser transport test. I’m now assembling the single-file build and checking how the full game behaves in the browser and AI Hub harness.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > ComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/build.py <<'EOF'\n#\"'!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Bundle local development modules into the single shareable game.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport re\n\nfolder = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nroot = folder.parent\nslug = folder.name\ncredits = json.loads((root / '\"'exit-interview.json').read_text())\nhtml = (folder / 'index.html').read_text()\nhtml = html.replace('<\"'!-- HUB_CLIENT -->'\"', '<script>\\\\n' + (folder / 'session.js').read_text() + '\\\\n</script>\\\\n' + '''<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"2-2\\\">\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Score three wrecks. Bank shots around cover and burst past incoming shells.\\\">\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Move: left stick / WASD. Aim: right stick / mouse. Fire: R2 / click. Burst: Circle or L2 / Space.\\\">\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">''')\nhtml = html.replace('/* STYLES */', (folder / 'styles.css').read_text())\nimports = \\\"import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\\\\nimport RAPIER from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3/+esm';\\\\n\\\"\nmodules = []\nfor name in ['audio.js', 'hub.js', 'sim.js', 'view.js', 'app.js']:\n    text = (folder / name).read_text()\n    text = re.sub(r'\"'^import .*?;'\"\\\\n', '', text, flags=re.M)\n    text = re.sub(r'\"'^export '\"', '', text, flags=re.M)\n    text = text.replace('// CREDITS_DATA', 'const CREDITS = ' + json.dumps(credits, ensure_ascii=False).replace('</', '<\\\\\\\\/') + ';')\n    modules.append(text)\nscript = imports + '\\\\n'.join(modules)\nhtml = html.replace('/* APP_MODULE */', script.replace('</script', '<\\\\\\\\/script'))\n(root / f'{slug}.html').write_text(html)\n(folder / 'bundled-module.js').write_text(script)\nprint(f'Built {slug}.html ({len(html.encode()):,} bytes)')\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nroot=Path('.')\ndata={\n'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-05 21:25:52','source':'Combat (Atari, 1977)','plan':'none','genre':'Arcade vehicular arena shooter','perspective':'Elevated orthographic third-person / top-down arena','tech':'Three.js 0.180.0 WebGPURenderer (WebGL2 fallback), Rapier 0.19.3, Gamepad API, Web Audio, WebRTC, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0; one HTML file with CDN engine dependencies','artDirection':'Procedural cel-shaded 3D tabletop diorama with ink outlines, cream paper, teal and vermilion','animation':'Three.js AnimationMixer and AnimationClip for treads, antenna and cannon recoil; procedural particles and motion','audio':'Code-synthesized funk music (10% default), effects, and Animalese-style formant gibberish voices; no audio files','online':'AI Hub shared-world two-player host-authoritative sessions; standalone direct WebRTC invitation/return codes; local two-player duel','testing':'Headless Chromium WebGPU, keyboard/mouse, emulated standard gamepads, multitouch, offline rendered audio, two-browser WebRTC and AI Hub harness; no physical devices','research':'none; native source knowledge only. Supplied AI Hub integration code and pinned engine distributions downloaded directly.','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra','usage':'added on import'},\n'testingFeedback':['unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown'],\n'engineFeedback':['Three.js combines custom procedural geometry, toon shading, orthographic cameras and native animation in one scene.','unknown','Tank simulation, arena rules, AI navigation, controller-first menus and authoritative network state.','unknown','none','A built-in controller-first UI and fixed-step gameplay layer would simplify small games.'],\n'promptFeedback':['The source constraints and complete vertical-slice requirements gave a clear creative target.','The prohibition on web research coexists with a required remote integration; I treated direct integration-code downloads as implementation, not source research.','Making the same complete game flow work with keyboard, controller, touch and network authority.','Specify whether manual WebRTC signaling is acceptable for standalone online play and whether a relay service is available.'],\n'aiHub':{'name':'ComBop','tagline':'Small tanks. Big comebacks.','description':'A playful ink-and-paper tank rumble inspired by Combat. Bank shells around corners, vanish in the ghost garden, and burst through a three-arena solo circuit or duel a friend.','type':'Game','genre':'Shooter','source':'Combat (1977)','series':'','players':'1–2','controls':'WASD / left stick move; mouse / right stick aim; click / R2 fire; Space / Circle / L2 burst; Esc / Options pause; touch drag to drive with assisted fire.','tags':['3d','arcade','versus','top-down','retro','vehicles']}}\n(root/'exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 ComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/build.py\nnode --check ComBop-Combat-1977-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212552/bundled-module.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
